      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Core idea: failover is a pre-planned, fenced ownership transfer to a warm shadow, not an emergency rebuild;\nhome regions stay authoritative, and the global layer is a pushed, static map so thin it cannot be the outage.",
