    {
      "id": "0oc4x3_ZsgHHBluszDQA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 535.68,
      "height": 580,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "as",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1666365236,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 758423049,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795134615905,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHAT CHANGES VS SENIOR\n- Senior: a global quorum DB is on the routing path of\n  every write; a slow quorum hurts every region.\n  Staff: the home region is authoritative for its LBs;\n  the global map only changes on failover. Routers\n  use a pushed, versioned copy (statically stable).\n- WARM by default: the backup region keeps a shadow\n  LB (config applied, certs present, 0 traffic, small\n  capacity). Failover = promote + scale, not create.\n- Cells inside a region: a cell outage moves only its\n  LBs; \"region down\" is just \"all cells down\".\n- Dependency audit: us-west-2 CP must not call\n  us-east-1 IAM, STS, KMS or DNS. TLS certs and keys\n  replicated in advance (multi-region keys).\n- Provider-driven evacuation: quorum signal + human\n  approval bulk-moves opted-in LBs, paced.\n\nTRADE-OFFS\n- WARM costs config footprint and capacity; COLD is\n  cheap but RTO is minutes and may hit capacity\n  limits during a regional event.\n- Async replication means RPO > 0. Sync would put the\n  backup region on every write path. Choose async and\n  show the restored config_version.\n- Senior design is fine while failovers are rare and\n  manual; move to staff for AUTO failover and RTO\n  commitments to large tenants.\nMigration: shadow configs for opted-in LBs, drills,\n  then make WARM the default tier.",
      "originalText": "WHAT CHANGES VS SENIOR\n- Senior: a global quorum DB is on the routing path of\n  every write; a slow quorum hurts every region.\n  Staff: the home region is authoritative for its LBs;\n  the global map only changes on failover. Routers\n  use a pushed, versioned copy (statically stable).\n- WARM by default: the backup region keeps a shadow\n  LB (config applied, certs present, 0 traffic, small\n  capacity). Failover = promote + scale, not create.\n- Cells inside a region: a cell outage moves only its\n  LBs; \"region down\" is just \"all cells down\".\n- Dependency audit: us-west-2 CP must not call\n  us-east-1 IAM, STS, KMS or DNS. TLS certs and keys\n  replicated in advance (multi-region keys).\n- Provider-driven evacuation: quorum signal + human\n  approval bulk-moves opted-in LBs, paced.\n\nTRADE-OFFS\n- WARM costs config footprint and capacity; COLD is\n  cheap but RTO is minutes and may hit capacity\n  limits during a regional event.\n- Async replication means RPO > 0. Sync would put the\n  backup region on every write path. Choose async and\n  show the restored config_version.\n- Senior design is fine while failovers are rare and\n  manual; move to staff for AUTO failover and RTO\n  commitments to large tenants.\nMigration: shadow configs for opted-in LBs, drills,\n  then make WARM the default tier.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "qcWlrlUKbtah-UWdbiz4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 680,
      "y": 920,
