      "updated": 1795134615905,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CORRECTNESS + FAILURE MODES\n- Fencing: every CP write carries the epoch; regional\n  stores reject epoch < current. The old home cannot\n  overwrite anything after it returns.\n- Lease: home renews its ownership lease (30 s);\n  failover needs lease expiry or quorum \"region down\"\n  + policy approval -> never two owners.\n- Workflow idempotent on (lb_id, epoch); resumes from\n  the failover_op record after a crash.\n- Partial failover: if us-west-2 fails, try the next\n  backup region; FAILING_OVER with no progress for\n  10 min -> page.\n- us-east-1 returns: reconcile job diffs fenced configs\n  vs new home; shows changes from the RPO window to\n  the customer, never auto-merges.\n- Herd control: admission queue per backup region,\n  token bucket per account, reserved capacity for\n  WARM tiers; others queue with an ETA.\n- Kill switch: freeze all AUTO failovers globally, so\n  a bad health signal cannot stampede the fleet.\n- Recovery: map rebuilt from directory snapshot +\n  ownership op-log replay.\n\nSLOs (assumed)\n- CP reads 99.99% during loss of 1 region\n- Failover RTO p99: WARM < 60 s, COLD < 10 min\n- Config RPO p99 < 5 s\n- Zero dual-owner incidents (tested in drills)",
      "originalText": "CORRECTNESS + FAILURE MODES\n- Fencing: every CP write carries the epoch; regional\n  stores reject epoch < current. The old home cannot\n  overwrite anything after it returns.\n- Lease: home renews its ownership lease (30 s);\n  failover needs lease expiry or quorum \"region down\"\n  + policy approval -> never two owners.\n- Workflow idempotent on (lb_id, epoch); resumes from\n  the failover_op record after a crash.\n- Partial failover: if us-west-2 fails, try the next\n  backup region; FAILING_OVER with no progress for\n  10 min -> page.\n- us-east-1 returns: reconcile job diffs fenced configs\n  vs new home; shows changes from the RPO window to\n  the customer, never auto-merges.\n- Herd control: admission queue per backup region,\n  token bucket per account, reserved capacity for\n  WARM tiers; others queue with an ETA.\n- Kill switch: freeze all AUTO failovers globally, so\n  a bad health signal cannot stampede the fleet.\n- Recovery: map rebuilt from directory snapshot +\n  ownership op-log replay.\n\nSLOs (assumed)\n- CP reads 99.99% during loss of 1 region\n- Failover RTO p99: WARM < 60 s, COLD < 10 min\n- Config RPO p99 < 5 s\n- Zero dual-owner incidents (tested in drills)",
      "fontSize": 16,
