      "updated": 1795134615905,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "STAFF SCOPE\n- Product: HA tiers (COLD / WARM / ACTIVE-ACTIVE),\n  priced; failover policy as config per LB.\n- Contract: we move the LB, not the backends' data.\n  Customers must run backends in the backup region.\n- Quotas: backup-region quota reserved per account\n  for WARM; COLD is best effort.\n- Game days: quarterly region-evacuation drill;\n  customer \"test failover\" against a sandbox copy.\n- Observability: per-LB failover timeline,\n  replication lag, ownership history in audit log.\n- Rollout: shadow replication first, then manual\n  failover API, then AUTO for opted-in tenants.\n- Cost: shadow configs + warm capacity per tier.\n\nQUESTIONS TO ASK\n- Is only the CP down, or the LB data plane too?\n- Must the LB keep the same DNS name / IPs?\n- Manual switch only, or automatic failover too?\n- Are backends already running in a backup region?\n- Acceptable RTO, and RPO for config changes?\n- Can certs and keys leave the home region?\n- Who declares a region down: us or the customer?",
      "originalText": "STAFF SCOPE\n- Product: HA tiers (COLD / WARM / ACTIVE-ACTIVE),\n  priced; failover policy as config per LB.\n- Contract: we move the LB, not the backends' data.\n  Customers must run backends in the backup region.\n- Quotas: backup-region quota reserved per account\n  for WARM; COLD is best effort.\n- Game days: quarterly region-evacuation drill;\n  customer \"test failover\" against a sandbox copy.\n- Observability: per-LB failover timeline,\n  replication lag, ownership history in audit log.\n- Rollout: shadow replication first, then manual\n  failover API, then AUTO for opted-in tenants.\n- Cost: shadow configs + warm capacity per tier.\n\nQUESTIONS TO ASK\n- Is only the CP down, or the LB data plane too?\n- Must the LB keep the same DNS name / IPs?\n- Manual switch only, or automatic failover too?\n- Are backends already running in a backup region?\n- Acceptable RTO, and RPO for config changes?\n- Can certs and keys leave the home region?\n- Who declares a region down: us or the customer?",
